"""The guiding-centre blocks for the Pyccel kernels, inlined where they are called.

The Pyccel version of ``guiding_centre.cuh`` (CUDA) and of `mpiparticles.kernels.guiding_centre`
(NumPy and Metal), with the same arithmetic. A Pyccel kernel, also of another package, imports
them::

    from mpiparticles.kernels.guiding_centre_pyccel import gc_rates, gc_velocity

and cunumpy's kernel cache (``PyccelCache``) builds this module with the kernel; Pyccel
inlines the calls. The functions have no local variables (inlined into a loop under
``#$ omp parallel for``, Pyccel would declare them outside the loop, shared by the
threads), so every subexpression is written out; the C compiler computes the repeated ones
once. Generated by ``_generate_guiding_centre_pyccel.py``; edit that, not this file.
"""

from math import sqrt

